1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,120
The fan!

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:04,400
Pass him on the left!

3
00:00:04,639 --> 00:00:05,440
Step on it!

4
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:06,719
Now pass him on the right!

5
00:00:07,160 --> 00:00:08,359
Look out for the wall!

6
00:00:08,480 --> 00:00:09,599
Hit the brakes!

7
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:13,320
Why didn't you hit the brakes?

8
00:00:13,519 --> 00:00:15,280
He was just too scared!

9
00:00:15,439 --> 00:00:17,120
What do you mean too scared?

10
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:19,199
Something got into my eyes.

11
00:00:19,240 --> 00:00:20,400
Those were your hands.

12
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:21,240
My turn.

13
00:00:21,679 --> 00:00:23,559
Let me show you how it's really done.

14
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:27,400
Oh, what's wrong with the computer?

15
00:00:27,519 --> 00:00:29,960
Oh, it's been really acting up for a while.

16
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
It turns off by itself. It's no big deal. I just turn it back on.

17
00:00:34,119 --> 00:00:35,719
I don't like this at all.

18
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:38,519
Come on, Nolik, let's go inside and take a look.

19
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:43,880
Just like people, machines can get sick too.

20
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:48,280
They can get a very high temperature and even start coughing and sneezing.

21
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:53,079
And if a machine or an appliance gets seriously sick,

22
00:00:53,359 --> 00:00:56,280
sometimes it can be too late to fix them at all.

23
00:00:56,280 --> 00:01:00,640
So wouldn't it be better if we could keep them from getting sick in the first place?

24
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:06,879
Everybody knows that people who look after their health get sick less often and live longer.

25
00:01:06,879 --> 00:01:09,000
And the same goes for machines.

26
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,719
Machines break less often and live longer if they're properly taken care of.

27
00:01:13,719 --> 00:01:19,159
That's why machines need to be checked from time to time, and cleaned, and oiled.

28
00:01:19,159 --> 00:01:23,359
And that's what's called preventive maintenance.

29
00:01:23,359 --> 00:01:29,959
And preventive maintenance is something that always should be kept in mind by humans and by Fixies.

30
00:01:42,439 --> 00:01:43,400
Oh, what is that?

31
00:01:44,439 --> 00:01:45,400
What is what?

32
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:46,920
Can you hear that?

33
00:01:47,079 --> 00:01:49,079
What are all those sounds?

34
00:01:49,319 --> 00:01:50,719
It's probably just… um…

35
00:01:51,359 --> 00:01:53,039
a Fixie eater that woke up.

36
00:01:53,359 --> 00:01:55,599
What? What do you mean, Fixie-eater?

37
00:01:55,879 --> 00:02:02,280
Didn't you know that inside of some appliances there live horrible monsters?

38
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:07,159
They love to attack Fixies and eat them up!

39
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:14,560
And the smaller the Fixies are, the more the Fixie-eater likes to eat them!

40
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:19,960
And how come you never told me anything about Fixie-eaters before?

41
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:23,319
I didn't want you to get scared!

42
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:30,480
All right, Scaredy Cat, let's keep going.

43
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:42,280
Simka, where are you?

44
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:01,780
Oh, no! Don't eat me, Fixie-eater!

45
00:03:05,900 --> 00:03:09,680
Oh! Simka! Come over here!

46
00:03:09,939 --> 00:03:11,939
The sound is coming from here! Take a look!

47
00:03:11,939 --> 00:03:13,819
It's not a Fixie-eater at all!

48
00:03:14,060 --> 00:03:15,579
It's just a fan!

49
00:03:16,020 --> 00:03:18,219
Not just Nolik, it needs our help!

50
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:20,060
See how sick that fan is?

51
00:03:20,219 --> 00:03:22,699
Let's go and get it working! Right now!

52
00:03:24,699 --> 00:03:28,259
A computer can only run when all of its parts are working.

53
00:03:28,419 --> 00:03:32,939
And even though a fan looks like nothing more than a simple little engine with a propeller,

54
00:03:33,060 --> 00:03:34,939
the computer couldn't work without it.

55
00:03:35,139 --> 00:03:40,780
It has the very important job of keeping all of those other parts cool when they start heating up.

56
00:03:41,539 --> 00:03:45,419
It cools down the inside of a computer by blowing a stream of air.

57
00:03:45,539 --> 00:03:48,539
But if the fan gets dirty and starts working poorly,

58
00:03:48,620 --> 00:03:51,539
the computer might get overheated and turn off.

59
00:03:51,740 --> 00:03:53,740
Or it can simply break!

60
00:03:57,539 --> 00:03:59,180
You have to turn off your computer!

61
00:03:59,259 --> 00:04:00,020
How come?

62
00:04:00,099 --> 00:04:01,379
I'll tell you later!

63
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:15,800
That part's done. Now we oil it.

64
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:18,000
Let me try!

65
00:04:18,100 --> 00:04:19,500
Alright!

66
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:24,900
It's oiled up!

67
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,500
Just like your nose!

68
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:27,600
Tom Thomas!

69
00:04:27,700 --> 00:04:29,000
Turn it on!

70
00:04:31,779 --> 00:04:32,779
Tideesh!

71
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:41,900
And then suddenly I hear this terrible roar of a Fixie-eater!

72
00:04:42,139 --> 00:04:44,299
But I wasn't scared one little bit,

73
00:04:44,419 --> 00:04:47,219
and I just ran right into the battle!

74
00:04:47,339 --> 00:04:48,139
And Simka?

75
00:04:48,139 --> 00:04:50,019
Oh, she was hiding somewhere.

76
00:04:50,019 --> 00:04:52,699
You know, she's a girl and they're all cowards.

77
00:04:52,779 --> 00:04:56,219
So I had to fight the monster all by myself.

78
00:04:58,579 --> 00:05:03,299
Oh, I guess that was an example of how girls hide like cowards when they're too scared.

79
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:05,739
Well, um…

80
00:05:05,859 --> 00:05:06,500
Yeah!

